<p><strong>D/Annie Liontas</strong> is the trans-genderqueer author of the memoir <a href="https://bookshop.org/a/132/9781668085561" class="external" target="_blank"><em>Sex with a Brain Injury: On Concussion and Recovery</em></a>, which won the ALA’s 2025 Stonewall Award for Nonfiction and the 2025 Lambda Literary Córdova prize, as well as the novel <a href="https://bookshop.org/a/132/9781476789095" class="external" target="_blank"><em>Let Me Explain You</em></a>. Their work has appeared in <em>The Atlantic</em>, <em>The New York Times Book Review</em>, <em>The New Review</em>, <em>Oprah Daily</em>, and elsewhere. An Assistant Professor at Lehigh University, Liontas helped secure a Mellon Foundation grant on Disability Justice to bring storytelling to communities in the criminal justice system. They write the Most Anticipated Queer Books list at <em>Electric Literature</em> and live in Philadelphia with their wife, dog, and Email the rabbit.</p>
