<p><strong>Maria Adelmann</strong> is the author of a new novel, <a href="https://bookshop.org/a/132/9781668089972" class="external" target="_blank"><em>The Adjunct</em></a>, as well as the story collection <a href="https://bookshop.org/a/132/9780316450812" class="external" target="_blank"><em>Girls of a Certain Age</em></a> and the novel <a href="https://bookshop.org/a/132/9780316450850" class="external" target="_blank"><em>How to Be Eaten</em></a>, an NPR book of the year and Belletrist book club pick. She has written for <em>Tin House</em>, <em>n+1</em>, <em>Electric Literature</em>, <em>The New York Times</em>, and many others, and her writing has been distinguished by <em>The Best American Short Stories</em>. She has worked variously as a hotel reviewer, product tester, and copywriter and currently lives in Philadelphia.</p>
