<p><strong>Chet’la Sebree</strong> is the author of the debut essay collection <a href="https://bookshop.org/a/132/9780593595848" class="external" target="_blank"><em>Turn (W)here: A Geography of Home</em></a> as well the poetry collections <a href="https://bookshop.org/a/132/9781963108460" class="external" target="_blank"><em>Blue Opening</em></a>, longlisted for PEN/Voelcker Award for Poetry and a finalist for both the <em>Los Angeles Times</em> Book Prize and the Lambda Literary Award for Bisexual Poetry; <a href="https://bookshop.org/a/132/9780374539023" class="external" target="_blank"><em>Field Study</em></a>, winner of the James Laughlin Award; and <a href="https://bookshop.org/a/132/9781936970629" class="external" target="_blank"><em>Mistress</em></a>, nominated for an NAACP Image Award. Currently, she’s an associate professor at the George Washington University.</p>
