					<div class="bio">
						<h4>D/Annie Liontas</h4>
												<p>D/Annie Liontas is the trans-genderqueer author of the memoir <em>Sex with a Brain Injury: On Concussion and Recovery</em>, which won the ALA’s 2025 Stonewall Award for Nonfiction and the 2025 Lambda Literary Córdova prize, as well as the novel <em>Let Me Explain You</em>. Their work has appeared in <em>The Atlantic</em>, <em>The New York Times Book Review</em>, <em>The New Review</em>, <em>Oprah Daily</em>, and elsewhere. An Assistant Professor at Lehigh University, Liontas helped secure a Mellon Foundation grant on Disability Justice to bring storytelling to communities in the criminal justice system. They write the Most Anticipated Queer Books list at <em>Electric Literature</em> and live in Philadelphia with their wife, dog, and Email the rabbit.</p>
